</ul><h1>A Perfect Solution</h1><p>One of the first things we sell? A speaker dock. It charges your phone and amplifies it! What more could you want?</p>
<p>It turns out: a lot. Speaker docks are stupid and outdated. We make that point ourselves.</p>
<p>So then we sell charging cables and leave the amplification to an array of bluetooth speakers. Is that good enough for you?</p>
<p>No!</p>
<p>“They charge my phone too slowly,” you say. “It takes FOREVER!”</p>
<p>Fine. We get our hands on some cables and wall blocks that charge phones fast. Like, really fast. This, surely, should be what you’re after. Right?</p>
<p>Absolutely not. Sure, it can get your iPhone up and running in record time, but what if you want to use your phone <em>at this very instant</em>? “I had to unplug it,” you say, “and then I forgot to plug it back in. And now my phone is DEAD! AGAIN! And I was expecting an IMPORTANT CALL! You’ve ruined my life, Meh!”</p>
<p>But don’t worry. We have plans to make it up to you. We offer charging <em>pads</em>. You don’t need to remember to re-insert the plug anymore! You can just set it down on the pad when you need a little juice.</p>
<p>Did we nail it?</p>
<p>Not at all. What if you want to sit in the chair that’s nowhere <em>near</em> an outlet, you say.</p>
<p>Not a problem! We get our hands on these things: power banks that can provide wireless charging. Set it down wherever, and there you go: a charging pad sans plug-in. And if you want to say, “Yeah, but what if it dies?” that’s why we’re selling a two-pack. You can always have one charged and ready to go.</p>
<p>So, did we finally solve the riddle of charging convenience?</p>
<p>Probably not! You’re probably gonna say, “But Meh, what if I want to–”</p>
