<p>“Honey? What’s wrong?” It was the copywriter’s wife. She stood in the doorway to his home office, a look of concern on her face.</p>
<p>The copywriter turned from his laptop in a daze. “Huh? What?”</p>
<p>“You’re yelling,” said the copywriter’s wife.</p>
<p>“I was? What about?”</p>
<p>“Charging stuff,” said the copywriter’s wife. “Were you arguing, honey? With the customers in your head?”</p>
<p>The copywriter smiled and shook his head. “Of course not, dear. I would never do something like that!”</p>